      "math_academy_id": "q-129549",
      "knowledge_point_id": "16601513-9b74-5cec-9af6-2d99b98e1ab3",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Repeated Integral",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $x+y=u,$ $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{y}^{1+y}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{y}^{1+y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{y+1}+\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{y+1}){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
