      "knowledge_point_id": "d237f9fb-b5d2-53e0-bc28-ee50d9e08852",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Rectangular Domain",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:        \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}48{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}48{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =[16{y}^{3}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =16({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$",
