      "problem": "Which of the following gives the value of the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,2]\\times [0,\\pi ]?$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\,{x}^{1/2}\\,{y}^{1/2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})\\text{ }(\\sqrt{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
